course: dictionary
lesson: 15764
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «The band played loud trumpets at the parade.» Here trumpets are instruments, the brass things you blow into to make music.
explain: «The elephant trumpets loudly by the river.» Now trumpets is a verb, something the elephant does. It makes a loud call. You can spot this because the sentence is about one animal doing an action.
explain: «Trumpets sounded as the queen entered the hall.» Here trumpets means a loud fanfare, a grand musical call that tells everyone an important person has arrived. The clues are queen, entered and hall.
fact: «Trumpets» (noun) means more than one trumpet, a brass musical instrument you blow into.
fact: «Trumpets» (verb) means makes a loud call, as an elephant does. It goes with he, she or it.
fact: «Trumpets sounded» means a loud fanfare was played to announce someone.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word and see if the sentence still makes sense: «The elephant shouts loudly» fits, so trumpets is a verb there.
exercise: «The band played loud trumpets at the parade.» What are the trumpets here? | Animals that make a loud call | *Brass instruments you blow into | Long, thin roads | Small birds
exercise: «The elephant trumpets loudly by the river.» What is the elephant doing? | *Making a loud call | Playing a tune on a flute | Running very fast | Drinking water
exercise: «Trumpets sounded as the king arrived.» What do the trumpets announce? | A lunch break | The end of a football match | Rain is coming | *The arrival of an important person
test: «The children counted the trumpets before the concert.» What kind of word is trumpets here? | *Noun, meaning more than one instrument | Adjective | Verb | Adverb
test: «The baby elephant trumpets for its mum.» What does trumpets mean? | *Makes a loud call | Eats leaves | Blows a brass instrument softly | Is very tired
exam: «Trumpets sounded, and everyone turned to the stage.» What does trumpets mean here? | *A loud fanfare to announce someone | Soft music for sleeping | Cold winter weather | Rain on a roof
